I've added an expo config plugin, making this module compatible with the expo managed workflow. This does not mean it can be ran within expo go, since it still needs the native code, however you can create an expo dev-client to mimic expo go. 

To use it, all a user has to do is add the following in their app.json:

```{
"expo": {
    "plugins": [
      "react-native-android-auto"
    ]
  }
}
```

After this, they can use the module through javascript, just like in react native bare and the expo ejected workflow.

e2e test failed with multiple subSpaces found for a single spacerequest.

This PR replaces the subSpace name generation logic from using `GenerateName: parentSpace.Name-` to `Name: parentSpace.Name-subs`. 
In this way the name of the subSpace is predetermined and trying to create it more than once will fail. Also getting the subSpace now is simpler since we don't need to rely on listing the subSpaces by label anymore. 

**CAVEAT**: with this change there can be only 1 subSpace provisioned per each parentSpace. Previously using the generated name the relationship was 1 parentSpace - N subSpaces. 

Paired with: https://github.com/codeready-toolchain/toolchain-e2e/pull/735

Jira bug: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/SANDBOX-52

